course: dictionary
lesson: 6517
title: The Nenets, a people of the Arctic
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter often means a name, such as a people, a place or a language. Nenets is a name. The Nenets are a people, and Nenets is also the name of their language.
explain: «About four million people live in the Arctic, including Indigenous peoples such as the Inuit in Canada and Greenland, the Sámi in Norway, Sweden, Finland and Russia, and the Nenets in Russia.» The sentence lists the Nenets with other Indigenous peoples, so the Nenets must be a group of people who live in the Arctic.
explain: «Yet the Arctic was never empty: Inuit, Sámi, Nenets and other peoples have lived there for thousands of years.» The word «peoples» is a clue that Nenets names a group, not one person. Check it: swap in «a group of people» and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: The Nenets are a people of the Arctic in northern Russia.
fact: Traditionally, the Nenets herd reindeer.
fact: «Nenets» can also be the name of the language the Nenets people speak.
fact: The Arctic is the cold region around the North Pole, and Indigenous peoples have lived there for thousands of years.
fact: «The Nenets» means the whole people, and «a Nenets» means one person from that people.
exercise: Where do the Nenets live? | In the middle of Africa | On the islands of Japan | *In northern Russia | In southern Spain
exercise: Traditionally, what do the Nenets herd? | Cows | Goats | Sheep | *Reindeer
exercise: Which word in «Yet the Arctic was never empty: Inuit, Sámi, Nenets and other peoples have lived there for thousands of years» is the name of a people? | thousands | *Nenets | Arctic | empty
test: Besides a people, what else can Nenets mean? | *The language the Nenets speak | A cold wind | A month of the year | A kind of reindeer
test: In «The Nenets are an Indigenous people of the Arctic», what does Nenets refer to? | A place on a map | A river | *A people | A type of snow
exam: Which sentence uses Nenets as a language? | Nenets live on the tundra in Russia | The Nenets herd reindeer every winter | *She speaks Nenets with her grandmother | The Nenets walked far north with their herds
